    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite (the single AcceptanceTest with both new tests) passes with BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged owner deletion to a soft-delete. The change touches six files, each with small, cohesive edits:\n\n**Persistence / DTO surface**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean column and its `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()` accessors (new methods, no existing method modified).\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct maps it by name automatically (no mapper change needed).\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` column (test profile uses `ddl-auto=none`).\n- `db/hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 appended `FALSE` to the 10 seed owner rows so the positional inserts still match the column count.\n\n**Behaviour**\n- `function/owner/DeleteOwner.java` \u2014 instead of `delete(owner)`, sets `deleted = true` and `save`s, so the row is retained and the endpoint still returns 2xx.\n- `function/owner/RequireUniqueIdentity.java` and `RequireUniqueHousehold.java` \u2014 each skips owners flagged deleted (a one-line `continue` guard), so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match was soft-deleted.\n\nKept structural impact low: every edited method stays trivial (CC \u2248 1\u20134), no large class had an existing method grown, and behaviour was added as small guards / new accessors rather than reworking the create pipeline. A newly created owner defaults to `deleted = false`; `GET /api/owners/{id}` continues to return the owner afterwards with `deleted: true`.\n\nBoth new tests (`coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains`, `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`) pass, and the build is green.",
